{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_004: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion → acc 0.537), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over a strong unimodal baseline. Config_011 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean ablation of config_004 that removes only the RNA modality while keeping the same image encoder and profile setting. If image-only ViT-L achieves comparable accuracy (~0.53-0.54), it reveals that the RNA modality is not contributing meaningfully and we should redirect budget toward image-model optimization or simpler architectures. If it is substantially lower, it confirms that multimodal fusion is genuinely beneficial and justifies further investment in multimodal configurations. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the fundamental design choice (multimodal vs. unimodal) before spending further budget on fine-tuning fusion methods, aggregation, or profile settings that may be irrelevant if one modality dominates."
}

